import equational_theories.Definability.CloneExtra4

/-!
# What three elements have left to give

Every one of the 19683 magmas on `Fin 3` has now been enumerated and tested against every source
law with an open definability cell, with the clone of each grown to four hundred members. This is
the single certificate that came out, and the carrier is settled: there is nothing else on three
elements.

Three hundred and twenty-four operations is the largest clone family in this development. It is
affordable because the carrier is small -- the family itself costs nine entries a member, so it is
nothing, and what sets the ceiling is the `k x k` composition table at a hundred thousand entries.
Both are stored as `Array (Array Nat)` for the reason given in `CloneExtra5.lean`, and both are
cut into blocks of sixteen rows that are appended back together. Both the blocks and the raised
recursion limit are needed: the limit an array literal wants grows with the number of entries in
it, and the time it takes to elaborate grows faster than that, so one undivided literal of a
hundred thousand entries takes half an hour where twenty of five thousand take three minutes.

This file is generated by `genclone5.py`.
-/

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

open Law Law.MagmaLaw

namespace Magma

